module

public import Sheaf.RingTheory.PowerSeriesCohenFormallySmoothAdic
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.ZMod

/-!
# Adic formal smoothness of power series over fields and Cohen rings

Source: Stacks Project, More on Algebra, Lemma Tag 07NL
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-power-series-field-cohen-fs-adic).

## Main statements

* `MvPowerSeries.formallySmoothAdic_rat` (landed,
  lem-weil-pbc-power-series-cohen-formally-smooth-adic): the characteristic-zero clause.
* `MvPowerSeries.formallySmoothAdic_zmod`: the positive-characteristic clause, the only new one.
* `MvPowerSeries.formallySmoothAdic_int_of_isCohenRing` (landed,
  lem-weil-pbc-power-series-cohen-formally-smooth-adic): the Cohen-ring clause, at the ideal
  `(p, X₁, …, Xₙ)`.

Clauses (1) and (3) are word for word the two landed declarations of
`Sheaf.RingTheory.PowerSeriesCohenFormallySmoothAdic`, imported here and not restated.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

namespace MvPowerSeries

/-- A power series ring over a characteristic-`p` field is adically formally smooth over `𝔽_p`.
Source: Stacks Project, More on Algebra, Lemma Tag 07NL, clause (2).
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-power-series-field-cohen-fs-adic)

Proof: The maximal ideal is generated by the variables (lem-weil-pbc-power-series-local-ring).
For a square-zero test ideal `J` and a map `g` killing the `k`th power of the variable ideal,
lift each `g(X i)` to `d i`. Then `(d i)^(2*k) = 0`; the ideal `a` generated by these lifts has
`a^(n*(2*k-1)+1) = 0`, by pigeonhole, also for `n = 0` with exponent one. Both the target
and its quotient are complete for these nilpotent ideals. Lift the coefficient map on `K`
by lem-weil-pbc-field-char-p-nilpotent-lifting (Tag 0322). Extend it using
lem-weil-pbc-power-series-universal-property-complete and the chosen variable lifts.
Uniqueness in the quotient gives the required equality with `g`. Every ring map between
characteristic-`p` rings respects the unique `ZMod p`-algebra structures. This supplies every
lift required by def-weil-pbc-formally-smooth-adic. -/
theorem formallySmoothAdic_zmod (p : ℕ) [Fact (Nat.Prime p)]
    (K : Type u) [Field K] [CharP K p] (n : ℕ) :
    @Algebra.FormallySmoothAdic (ZMod p) (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K) _ _
      ((C.comp (ZMod.castHom (dvd_refl p) K)).toAlgebra)
      (Ideal.span (Set.range (fun i : Fin n ↦ (X i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K)))) := by
  sorry

end MvPowerSeries
